-- erwartet: D022
-- **The quantifier domain was decoration, and this is the shape that measured it.**
--
-- `messung/OFFEN-PRUEFER-UND-GRAMMATIK-2026-09-07.md` §1.1 wrote the finding at ONE domain
-- and asserted the other eight. On 2026-09-08 the differential was run at all nine, one
-- probe per domain, on `messung/proben/probe-neun-domaenen.gab`:
--
--     domain           | errors | hints | emit md5   | verdict
--     -----------------|--------|-------|------------|-----------
--     all NINE         | 0      | 0     | dbc3e06b   | DECORATION
--
-- **Nine of nine, and the C byte-identical in every row.** The binder came out of the
-- domain named and was used against a table the domain never mentioned, and no pass said
-- so -- not the checker, not the emitter, and not the proof channel, which translates the
-- BODY and never sees the domain that was supposed to bound the binder.
--
-- This file is the sharpest of the nine: `threads` names no place at all, so there is no
-- declaration for a rule to read and call wrong. The refusal has to say that there is
-- none.
module gift::domaene_schmuck {

const NGERAETE : u32 = 64;

table Topologie count NGERAETE {
    slot {
        bereich : u8,
    }

    -- `g` is drawn from the thread set and indexes the slots of a table. Nothing joins the
    -- two, and until 2026-09-08 nothing said so: `0 errors, 0 hints`, and the same C as
    -- `forall g in slots of Topologie`.
    invariant bereich_klein cost O(n) runs offline :
        forall g in threads : Topologie.slots[g].bereich <= 255;
}

}
